dist/
# setuptools' scratch tree. `python -m build --wheel --outdir /tmp/...` and a
# plain `pip install .` both write it into the SOURCE directory whatever
# --outdir says, so it appears the first time anyone follows the README or runs
# what ci.yml runs. Untracked and unignored, it is one `git add -A` away from a
# committed second copy of the whole package — including a stale plugin_pb2.py
# that would then outrank the real one in a reader's grep.
build/
